# ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-SSH-AGENT-AUTHORITY-RECON01: recon/contract ACT
# Successor slice to SEATBELT-NETWORK-EGRESS-RECON01 (unblocked by
# LIVE network-egress mechanism evidence, NOT by that ACT's closure;
# that ACT remains OPEN / POLICY_INTENT_UNBOUND). ENTRY_HEAD =
# 911d02177 (the commit that closed network-egress §4; the SSH
# live specimen is strong LIVE_PROVEN qualification evidence for
# NETWORK_EGRESS_PROCEEDED on a real ClineMM sandboxed execution
# path, and proves raw key reads remain denied by design). Status:
# CLOSED / PASS_SEATBELT_SSH_AGENT_AUTHORITY_PRODUCT_POLICY_REPAIR_V1.
# §5 corrected contract (post macOS Seatbelt + OpenSSH + factory
# reviewer trio, after `path-literal` correction): capability shape
# `sshAuthenticationAuthority: deny | agent`; SBPL emits `(allow
# system-socket (socket-domain AF_UNIX))` + `(allow network-outbound
# (remote unix-socket (path-literal "<resolved>")))` (path-literal
# is the Unix-socket selector's exact-match primitive per Apple
# Sandbox Guide v1.0; distinct from filesystem-operation `literal`;
# NOT `subpath`, which would widen to sibling sockets); env
# reintroduction of SSH_AUTH_SOCK via the explicit `allow` list
# (step 3 of materializeEnvironment wins over step 4); raw-key reads
# remain DENIED in both modes; readonly-identity-file mode OUT OF
# SCOPE for V1. Substrate gate: probeSeatbeltAvailability() round-trip
# (NOT file-presence alone); this VSCodium shell reports
# probeSeatbeltAvailability() === false; substrate-eligible shell
# (Terminal.app / iTerm2 / debug-harness) required for IMPLEMENTATION01
# RED. IMPLEMENTATION_RED = AUTHORIZED at RECON01 closure; follow-on
# executable ACT SEATBELT-SSH-AGENT-AUTHORITY-IMPLEMENTATION01 opened
# immediately per reviewer "GO_AFTER_ONE_BOUNDED_FIX" verdict; that
# ACT inherits §15 verbatim and may renegotiate only through RED
# evidence. The ACT file AND the evidence directory are bound by the
# epic ledger at .factory/epics/safe-yolo-seatbelt.md (current ACT
# ledger row), so both must survive a fresh clone.
#
# ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-SSH-AGENT-AUTHORITY-IMPLEMENTATION01: executable
# ACT. Status: OPEN / HIGH. Inherits the frozen contract from RECON01
# §15 (sshAuthenticationAuthority: deny | agent; path-literal
# exact-socket AF_UNIX authority; SSH_AUTH_SOCK reintroduced via env
# allow; raw-key reads denied in both modes). Primary load-bearing RED:
# `agent + valid SSH_AUTH_SOCK + substrate` → {child env has
# SSH_AUTH_SOCK, exact agent socket connect succeeds, sibling socket
# connect fails, ~/.ssh/id_rsa remains unreadable}. Substrate-eligible
# shell required (Terminal.app / iTerm2 / debug-harness). Bound by the
# epic ledger at .factory/epics/safe-yolo-seatbelt.md (current ACT
# ledger row + Open work entry) and the epic-board frontier row, so
# this ACT file must survive a fresh clone.
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-SSH-AGENT-AUTHORITY-RECON01.md
!/.factory/evidence/ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-SSH-AGENT-AUTHORITY-RECON01/
